The macOS-DroidVM k27 fixes (Droid-VM/macOS-DroidVM main, 2026-11-08) that apply to sheng, after the audit in
out/macos-work/AUDIT-droidvm-main.md:
- 0015/0024 union lookup: a covered path leading back into the union ends with ENOENT instead of looping; a name missing
  from a read-only union layer is looked up in the covered one for a create too (mkdir /dev gave EROFS).
- 0017 native 4K code signing: a 4K page wholly past codeLimit in the last 16K block validates NX, not tainted.
- 0022 exec-env=NAME:VAR=VALUE[,VAR=VALUE...] appends variables to one executable's environment.
- 0023 the root union reports MNT_ROOTFS in statfs, getfsstat and the vfs sysctls (fseventsd's global logger).
- 0038 vfs_flags hides the root union's MNT_UNION from kexts (Sandbox mds.sb); ".." of a firmlink target is the source's
  parent; the last component of a delete or rename is not followed through a firmlink. kern_exec.c's union check reads
  mnt_flag.
- 0041 a realtime computation past max_rt_quantum is held to it (coreaudiod's I/O thread on the 19.2 MHz counter).
- 0042 timebase-hz=24000000: a 24 MHz timebase for userspace over the 19.2 MHz counter (CoreAudio, Swift clocks).
- 0047 mmap places mappings it chooses on 16K boundaries (V8, PartitionAlloc).
- exit-trace: exit() calls the board's native_exit_trace (user frames of WindowServer and loginwindow by default).
- 0035 deny-exec=PATH[,PATH...]: mobileactivationd and cryptexd (no Secure Enclave identity, no grafted cryptexes) do not run. Ours:
  exec-stand-in=PATH runs a stand-in as the daemon's job, which closes every connection to its services (scripts/absent-service);
  plain EPERM left clients waiting for a reply forever (mdmclient, so the login; run41/run42).
- one device at "/": vnode_getattr, every getattrlist form (bulk entries, the real device id and fsid, volume attributes), proc_info
  and the vfs fsid lists give the union's device id and fsid for a file of the root volume under it. They leaked the root volume's
  own, which getfsstat hides, so CoreServices could not place those files (FileIDTreeGetVRefNumForDevice -36, run37/run38).

